Sorry for not being on topic, but I think this is a more optimal
solution for PC's.

I have created a 1.44 MB floppy boot disk that boots any PC into a
minimal FreeDOS operating system (beta 9 rc 5), extracts NetHack 3.43
for DOS (386+, including CWSDPMI.EXE) into a 16 MB RAMdrive, and runs
the game with custom DEFAULTS.NH settings. There are 283,648 bytes
free on the floppy, so early games could be played safely using the
disk as the save directory. By default, the 16 MB RAMdrive is used for
saved files, so these must be backed up to permanent storage before
shutting down.

Everything on this disk should be redistributable. An image of this
disk can also be burned to make a bootable CDR.

